course: dictionary
lesson: 13287
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning the writer means by reading the words around it. «Mum is grafting a branch of a pear tree onto an old apple tree.» Here grafting is a garden job, where you join a cut piece of one plant onto another so they grow together.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «The doctor used grafting to repair the skin after the bad burn.» The words doctor and burn tell you this is about medicine, where healthy skin is moved to heal a wound. Always ask: what is the topic of this sentence?
explain: Speakers in Britain also use grafting to mean hard work. «Dad has been grafting all day on the building site.» Nobody is joining plants or moving skin here. The words all day and building site show that grafting means working very hard, often at tiring jobs.
fact: Grafting means joining a piece cut from one plant onto another plant so that they grow together.
fact: In medicine, skin grafting means moving healthy skin from one part of the body to another to repair it.
fact: In British everyday talk, «grafting» means working very hard, and a «grafter» is a hard worker.
fact: Phrases to know: «skin grafting», «grafting a tree», and «hard graft».
fact: In the US, «graft» can also mean using power dishonestly to get money. The sentence around it will show which meaning is meant.
exercise: «Mum is grafting a branch of a pear tree onto an old apple tree.» What does grafting mean here? | Watering the plants with a hose | *Joining a cut piece of one plant onto another plant | Painting a garden fence | Cutting down a tree
exercise: «Dad has been grafting all day on the building site.» What does grafting mean here? | Playing a game with his friends | *Working very hard at tiring work | Sleeping in the sun | Driving to the shops
exercise: «The doctor used grafting to repair the skin after the bad burn.» Which words tell you this is about medicine? | all day and tired | pear and branch | garden and apple | *doctor and burn
test: «The gardener spent the morning grafting new branches onto the old cherry tree.» What is grafting in this sentence? | Sweeping up fallen leaves | Picking cherries from the tree | Digging a hole for a new tree | *Joining a cut branch onto another plant so they grow together
test: «Kai's mum is a grafter; she works long shifts at the factory and never stops.» What does grafter mean? | *A hard worker | A person who grows apples | A person who draws pictures | A person who sleeps a lot
exam: «The surgeon used skin grafting to repair Sam's knee, and then Sam had to rest.» What does skin grafting mean here? | Washing the skin with soap | Cutting the hair off the leg | *Moving healthy skin from one part of the body to another to repair it | Painting a picture on the knee
